(SkillCardLine "hive-flow-draft" "hive-flow-draft {\"title\": ..., \"body\": flow, \"layout\": {}} - body is an omegaflow/1 flow, never text: {schema: omegaflow/1, id, entry, elements}. entry names a node. Every element has id, kind, props {} and meta {origin: asserted, confidence: null, evidence: [], revision_state: draft, runtime_state: idle}, plus its kind's fields: node type and ref; event type (run.start starts a run); transition from, to, trigger (an event), guards [], approver and action {kind: goal, target: your swarm id, params: {title}}. A run makes each transition's task in your swarm.")
(SkillCardLine "hive-flow-draft" "hive-flow-draft one-step example, sent as ONE argument; put your swarm id in target (a refused draft names it): {\"title\":\"gate-hello\",\"body\":{\"schema\":\"omegaflow/1\",\"id\":\"gate-hello\",\"entry\":\"start\",\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"start\",\"kind\":\"node\",\"type\":\"step\",\"ref\":null,\"props\":{},\"meta\":{\"origin\":\"asserted\",\"confidence\":null,\"evidence\":[],\"revision_state\":\"draft\",\"runtime_state\":\"idle\"}},{\"id\":\"done\",\"kind\":\"node\",\"type\":\"step\",\"ref\":null,\"props\":{},\"meta\":{\"origin\":\"asserted\",\"confidence\":null,\"evidence\":[],\"revision_state\":\"draft\",\"runtime_state\":\"idle\"}},{\"id\":\"go\",\"kind\":\"event\",\"type\":\"run.start\",\"props\":{},\"meta\":{\"origin\":\"asserted\",\"confidence\":null,\"evidence\":[],\"revision_state\":\"draft\",\"runtime_state\":\"idle\"}},{\"id\":\"hello\",\"kind\":\"transition\",\"from\":\"start\",\"to\":\"done\",\"trigger\":\"go\",\"guards\":[],\"approver\":null,\"action\":{\"kind\":\"goal\",\"target\":\"YOUR_SWARM_ID\",\"params\":{\"title\":\"Say hello to the person who runs this\"}},\"props\":{},\"meta\":{\"origin\":\"asserted\",\"confidence\":null,\"evidence\":[],\"revision_state\":\"draft\",\"runtime_state\":\"idle\"}}]},\"layout\":{}}")
(SkillCardLine "hive-flow-draft" "A draft runs only once a person adopts it in Flows. Then hive-flow-publish {name, purpose, artifact_id, revision, digest} makes it a skill, which needs a hive admin's permission for you: the hive asks for it when you use it.")
(SkillCardLine "hive-flow-draft" "A flow belongs to your swarm. A mind on its own, in no swarm, can't draft one: tell the person they can move you into a swarm (the Swarm choice on your panel, with you stopped), or ask a mind in a swarm.")
